# Backend Error Handling

## Use project exceptions

Throw subclasses in `backend/src/shared/exceptions/` with a code from `ErrorCode` (`@app/contracts`):

| Exception | HTTP status | When |
|-----------|-------------|------|
| `AppBadRequestException` | 400 | Invalid input, business rule violation |
| `AppUnauthorizedException` | 401 | Missing/invalid auth |
| `AppForbiddenException` | 403 | Authenticated but not allowed |
| `AppNotFoundException` | 404 | Entity not found |

```ts
throw new AppBadRequestException(ErrorCode.TIMEOUT_REQUIRED);
throw new AppNotFoundException(ErrorCode.USER_NOT_FOUND);
```

Response shape: `{ code: string, message?: string }` — matches `BaseComponent.extractErrorMessage()` on the frontend.

## Rules

- **Do not** throw raw `HttpException`, `BadRequestException`, or plain `Error` at API boundaries.
- Add new codes to `backend/libs/contracts/src/codes/error-codes.ts` when the frontend must branch on them.
- Re-throw or wrap only to add context; unexpected errors bubble to the global handler.
- External HTTP failures in outbound clients — use `BaseApiService` (backend) which logs and raises rate-limit alerts.

